+<!-- CARROT:REVIEW reviewed-for="d3d22721b59cc9cdf1dbcdbe62337ee11b9862b94bc02cbd7802be74fa392f66" reviewed-at="2026-10-29T09:00:00Z" -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN BEHAVIOR -->
+### Behavior
+
+OFF selects common TF1–TF4; ON shares Porter GAP1–4 between the Porter II EV conventional-cruise planner and button deceleration/optional low-target cancellation. Existing speed, mode and deceleration adjustments remain. In either mode, a clear projected gap and expired deceleration hold permit RES+ before vehicle speed falls to the lowered stock setting, bypassing the extra 0.5s reversal dwell. Brief opening of a close lead retains confirmation.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END BEHAVIOR -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN USAGE -->
+### Usage
+
+Enable in Porter Only, then adjust the dedicated gaps and lookahead. Allow about five seconds for planner refresh; neither set of saved values is copied or reset.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END USAGE -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN REFERENCE -->
+### Reference
+
+GAP selection buttons and model-stop/navigation targets remain. Settings do not guarantee physical spacing, braking or stopping.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END REFERENCE -->
 <!-- CARROT:MANUAL:END PorterGapUse -->
 
 <!-- CARROT:SETTING:END PorterGapUse -->
